course: dictionary
lesson: 6467
title: Nationalist: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nationalist is a person who strongly believes their nation should rule itself, or who thinks their own country is more important than others. A nation is a group of people who share a country, a history or a language, so start there when you meet the word.
explain: Read the clues in «a nationalist party». News about Scotland, Wales or Catalonia uses this phrase. The word party tells you it is a group, and the idea of self-rule tells you what the group wants. Check by swapping in your meaning: «a party that wants its nation to rule itself» still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Notice the job the word does. As a noun it names a person, as in «Scottish nationalists». As an adjective it describes things, as in «a nationalist movement». A capital N, as in «the Nationalists of Chiang Kai-shek», is a clue that the word names a specific group.
fact: Nationalism is the belief that a nation should rule itself, or that its own nation is more important than others.
fact: «Nationalist» can be a noun (a nationalist) or an adjective (nationalist), so look at the job the word does in the sentence.
fact: In Northern Ireland, a nationalist is a person who wants Northern Ireland to join the rest of Ireland.
fact: Nationalist leaders helped countries win independence, but nationalism has also been used to stir up hatred of other nations, as in some wars of the 20th century.
fact: «The Nationalists» was the name of Chiang Kai-shek's government in China, and after the civil war it retreated to Taiwan in 1949.
exercise: In «a nationalist party», what does nationalist mean? | *A party that wants its nation to rule itself | A party for people who love cooking | A party that sells land | A party with no members
exercise: Which word names a political group in «both the Nationalists of Chiang Kai-shek and the Communists did»? | Teacher | Japan | Mei | *Nationalists
exercise: Which sentence uses nationalist to mean a person? | A nationalist movement grew quickly | The nationalist flag was red | A nationalist party met on Monday | *A nationalist believes their nation should rule itself
test: After the civil war, what did the «Nationalist government» do? | They joined the People's Republic | *They retreated to Taiwan | They ruled Beijing | They ended the war in Japan
test: What does a nationalist in Northern Ireland want? | To sell all its land | *To join the rest of Ireland | To close its schools | To remove all rivers
exam: What is the best way to check the meaning of nationalist in «a nationalist party»? | Skip the sentence and move on forever | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters in the word | Ask someone else and stop reading
